From: Mercury worker lane 14 (Home Dashboard briefing)
Subject: Integrate source-backed dashboard briefing navigation into UnifiedHomePage

Context
=======
Lane 14 added source-backed TODAY agenda and RECENT WORK briefing sections to the Home
dashboard (Dashboard.cui + NewDashboardPage.Briefing.cs). The briefing rows route through a
typed, authority-checked target: `NewDashboardPage.TryNavigateBriefing(DashboardBriefingTarget)`.
The page exposes a `BriefingNavigator` delegate that a host sets to actually navigate. The
desktop host seam is `UnifiedHomePage` (READ ONLY for this lane). This patch is the exact seam
integration for the root coordinator to reconcile; it is intentionally NOT applied by this worker.

Important constraints honoured here:
- No arbitrary URI acceptance: an entity deep link is emitted only for the verified conversation
  route (`9to1://spaces/chat/{id}`). Every other kind either routes to its owning app surface or
  fails with a truthful refusal (the page then reports "this item's owning app is not reachable").
- No UI automation, no duplicated entity creation, no mutation of task status or external actions.
- The target Id/Kind/ActionKey are already validated by the page before the navigator is invoked,
  so this seam only maps a validated target to a navigation address.

